mapping "V2530.1" source="V2530" target="10298002" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source V2530 = Swedish extension of WHO V25.3 (person injured while boarding/alighting from
        motorcycle, in collision with railway train/vehicle), activity-context suffix SNOMED CT 10298002.
        Source definition: person boarding/alighting a motorcycle, train-collision context, sport
        activity. WHO V25.3 has three Athena targets: 438310 (motorcycle rider traffic victim), 440896
        (Railway accident, SNOMED CT 213770003), 4053428 (Accident while boarding/alighting from motor
        vehicle on road, SNOMED CT 242107006). Primary target chosen 438310 (motorcycle-rider victim) as
        the most clinically specific single concept; it captures the motorcycle+rider axis. Source
        bundles train + boarding/alighting + activity context, so any single target is
        broader-than-source; multi-target was considered but the cleaner single-best mapping is recorded
        here per the rubric's prefer-one-strongest guidance for non-combination sources. Low tier :
        broader mapping with multi-axis specificity loss; activity-context suffix has no representation.
        No web research; Athena-local mirror only.
        """
}
